Gives a custom geometry source the same request tracking as 0051 gives a
custom vector source. The loader kept a cancelled tile registered, and took a
registered tile to mean that the host had already been asked for it, so the
source told the host to cancel the tile and never asked for it again
(https://github.com/maplibre/maplibre-native-ffi/issues/778). Erasing the
registration on cancel instead dropped the other wrapped copies of the tile
and left its cached data behind.

Now each canonical tile has subscribers, identified by their actor, and a flag
for whether a fetch is in flight. A cancelled tile stays subscribed, so it
fetches again when it is next needed, and its cached data goes once the last
subscriber is destroyed. Copies of a tile share one fetch, and the host hears
a cancel once no copy needs the tile. Needs 0051 for ActorRef's operator==.
Upstream: not proposed. maplibre/maplibre-native#4928 took the earlier approach
and was closed.

